Debit does not mean bad. Credit does not mean good. Neither one means money in or money out, and neither one means plus or minus. Almost everyone learns this the wrong way round because of their bank messages.

This video covers the system underneath accounting: what an account actually is, what the chart of accounts is, what debit and credit really mean, and one rule, AED-LIC, that tells you which side to use. Then four quick drills, one full entry start to finish, and why your bank seems to say the opposite of everything you just learned. No ERPNext screens in this one.

If you were taught the three golden rules of accounting, AED-LIC gets you to the same answer by a different route. It works off the five kinds of accounts rather than real, personal and nominal.

